

[] split_flows.py: splitting may leave a tiny short line
- symptom: huc 12090205, HydroID 25050054 (0.7m), feature_id 5781811. for the entire HUC8, stream network derived from TauDEM has only 2 reaches with length 3.1m. other lines are >50m. so this 0.7m little guy is generated by split_flows.py
- cause: lake polygons do not align with dem-derived flowlines well, creating segmented flowlines, some very short
- assumption: I assume the purpose of overlaying the lake polygons is to split a flowline into 3 parts at most: the part before the inlet point to the lake; the part in the lake, and the part starts from the outlet to the end of the flow line.

[] test case: 12090205 full output
- flowline
ogrinfo -dialect sqlite -sql "select * from demDerived_reaches where LINKNO=485" demDerived_reaches.shp
- lake
ogrinfo -dialect sqlite -sql "select * from nwm_lakes_proj_subset where newID=5781691" nwm_lakes_proj_subset.gpkg 


